---
import LegalPage from '../../../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import t from '../../../data/en.json';
import site from '../../../data/site.json';
const description = 'Privacy policy of Ebmeyer Consulting, Nadine Ebmeyer, Cham ZG. No cookies, hosting in Switzerland, privacy-friendly audience measurement, your rights under the FADP and GDPR.';
---
<LegalPage locale="en" t={t} title="Privacy Policy" slug="privacy" altSlug="datenschutz" description={description}>
  <p class="legal__meta">
    Ebmeyer Consulting · Nadine Ebmeyer · Langackerstrasse 11 · 6330 Cham ZG · Switzerland<br />
    Version: September 2026
  </p>

  <p>
    This privacy policy explains which personal data Ebmeyer Consulting processes, for what
    purpose, and which rights you have. It applies to visits to the website
    <strong>ebmeyer-consulting.ch</strong> as well as to enquiries and to the collaboration
    in the context of consulting, training and speaking services.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is based on the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP) and, where applicable,
    the European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). The
    <a href="/en/terms/">General Terms and Conditions</a> refer to this policy for all
    matters of data protection.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting<br />
    Nadine Ebmeyer<br />
    Langackerstrasse 11<br />
    6330 Cham ZG, Switzerland<br />
    E-mail: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. No cookies, no tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and stores nothing in your browser. No
    visitor profiles are created, there is no tracking across devices or websites, and no
    advertising networks are embedded. Fonts and images are served directly from this
    website, not from third parties.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because no cookies are set and no services requiring consent are embedded, this website
    needs no cookie banner. You can use it in full without agreeing to any data
    processing.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Audience measurement with Plausible Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    For simple audience measurement this website uses <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong>,
    a privacy-friendly service provided by Plausible Insights OÜ, Estonia. Data is
    collected and stored exclusively on servers within the European Union. No analytics
    data is transferred to the United States and no cookies are used.
  </p>
  <p>Only aggregated, anonymous information is collected:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>pages visited and number of page views</li>
    <li>referring website, such as a search engine or LinkedIn</li>
    <li>country, derived from the IP address</li>
    <li>device type, browser and operating system</li>
    <li>clicks on outbound links, such as the booking link</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Your IP address is not stored.</strong> It is used only momentarily, together
    with a random value that changes daily, to form an irreversible checksum. This allows
    repeat visits within a single day to be counted without any possibility of identifying
    you. Recognition beyond that day is not possible.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is the legitimate interest in a data-minimising statistical analysis of
    website usage (Art. 31 FADP and Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Further details are set out in the
    <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible data policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Hosting and server log files</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by <strong>{site.legal.hostName}</strong>, Rapperswil-Jona
    ({site.legal.hostCountryEn}). The servers are located exclusively in Switzerland. No
    personal data is transferred abroad when you visit this website. The connection is
    encrypted end to end (TLS).
  </p>
  <p>
    When the website is accessed, the hosting provider processes technically necessary
    connection data such as IP address, date and time of access, page requested, browser
    type and operating system. This data serves solely the secure and stable operation of
    the website and the prevention of attacks. It is not merged with other data sources
    and is retained only as long as necessary for that purpose.
  </p>
  <p>
    A data processing agreement under Swiss data protection law is in place with
    {site.legal.hostName}. The domain <strong>ebmeyer-consulting.ch</strong> is likewise
    registered with {site.legal.registrarName} in {site.legal.registrarCountryEn}.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Booking a call via Calendly</h2>
  <p>
    To book an introductory call, this website links to the external service Calendly. The
    service is <strong>not embedded in this website</strong>: no data is sent to Calendly
    until you actively click the link and open Calendly's page. From that point, Calendly's
    privacy policy applies (Calendly LLC, USA). The details you enter there (name, e-mail
    address, preferred time) are used solely to hold the call.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Getting in touch</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us by e-mail or phone, your details are stored to handle the enquiry and
    any follow-up questions. This data is not passed on to third parties without your
    consent. Enquiries that do not lead to a collaboration are deleted after a reasonable
    period.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data in the course of a collaboration</h2>
  <p>
    Once an engagement is agreed, Ebmeyer Consulting processes the personal data required
    for it: name, company, role, contact details, correspondence, and contract and invoicing
    data. The purpose is to prepare quotations, perform the contract, issue invoices and
    maintain the business relationship. The legal basis is the performance of the contract
    (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and the legitimate interest in orderly business administration.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting <strong>does not process personal data on behalf of clients</strong>.
    The service model is designed so that clients set up and operate their AI applications
    themselves and on their own responsibility; control over the data remains with them.
    Sensitive personal data is processed only where this has been expressly agreed in
    writing.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Service providers and AI tools</h2>
  <p>
    For its own service delivery, Ebmeyer Consulting uses service providers, for example
    for e-mail, file storage, video calls, appointment booking and invoicing, as well as
    artificial intelligence tools. These providers receive only the data required for the
    respective service and are contractually bound to confidentiality.
  </p>
  <p>
    No confidential client data, no sensitive personal data and no professional or
    official secrets are entered into AI systems unless expressly agreed. Content from the
    collaboration is not released for the training of AI models.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Disclosure abroad</h2>
  <p>
    Visiting this website does not trigger any transfer of personal data abroad. Individual
    service providers under Section 8 may be based, or operate servers, outside
    Switzerland, including in countries without an adequate level of data protection. In
    such cases the disclosure is based on an adequacy decision of the Swiss Federal
    Council, on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses with the amendments
    required for Switzerland, or on a recognised certification scheme.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data security</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting takes appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect
    personal data against loss, misuse and unauthorised access: encrypted transmission,
    access protection on all devices and accounts, and restriction of access to the people
    needed for the collaboration.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data is retained only as long as necessary for the respective purpose.
    Business correspondence, contracts and accounting records are subject to the statutory
    retention period of ten years (Art. 958f of the Swiss Code of Obligations). Once the
    retention periods expire, the data is deleted or anonymised.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Links to third parties and social media</h2>
  <p>
    This website contains links to external services such as LinkedIn and Instagram. These
    services are not embedded; no data flows to them unless you click the respective link.
    The privacy policies of the respective providers apply to the linked services.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under applicable data protection law you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>information about the data processed about you</li>
    <li>correction of inaccurate data</li>
    <li>deletion of your data, unless a retention obligation applies</li>
    <li>restriction of processing</li>
    <li>receipt of your data in a common electronic format (data portability)</li>
    <li>objection to processing</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You also have the
    right to lodge a complaint with the Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information
    Commissioner (FDPIC) or, where the GDPR applies, with a supervisory authority in the EU.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting may amend this privacy policy at any time, for example when the
    services used or the legal situation change. The version published on this website at
    the time applies.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
